[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-6f8ba8e6-c701-4264-aa7f-d8e7d0a8bb01\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research papers</p><strong>Wed 7 Oct 2026 15:48 - 16:06 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/issta-2026/splash-issta-2026-venue-junior-ballroom-3%264\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Junior Ballroom 3&amp;4</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers#program\" class=\"navigate\">Testing and Analysis Tooling</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/jonathanbell\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Jonathan Bell</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"6f8ba8e6-c701-4264-aa7f-d8e7d0a8bb01\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>Integrating Multiple Features for Weakly-Supervised False-Passing Products Detection in Software Product Lines</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>Software Product Lines (SPL) enable the efficient development of configurable systems through feature modularization. However, the inherent configurability of software introduces significant challenges for fault localization within these systems. A key challenge among these is the problem of false-passing products, configurable products that contain faulty code yet coincidentally pass all their associated tests, thereby masking faults and misleading diagnosis efforts. To mitigate the negative impact of false-passing products. Supervised detection approaches are often impractical due to their reliance on complete labels, which are unavailable during early testing phases. To address this, we propose PULP, a label-agnostic detection approach that exploits the execution similarity between failing and false-passing products. PULP extracts five categories of features and employs a weakly-supervised learning algorithm to identify false-passing products without pre-labeled data. Evaluated on 823 buggy versions from six real-world SPL systems, PULP achieves superior detection performance, with best accuracy of 90.33% and precision of 94.93% for false-passing products and consistently enhances fault localization rankings after eliminating the negative impact of false-passing product. This method offers a practical tool for SPL testing and debugging in label-incomplete environments.</p>\n<p></p><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/taozhang2\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Tao Zhang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Chongqing University, China</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/yanlei\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Yan Lei\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/yanlei/e7481239-26a2-49a5-a150-5804fd3148fc/micro-avatar?1792875590000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Yan Lei<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Chongqing University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/haoranxia\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Haoran Xia<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Chongqing University, China</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/huanxie1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Huan Xie<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Southwest University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/chunyanliu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Chunyan Liu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Chongqing University</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/121/Integrating-Multiple-Features-for-Weakly-Supervised-False-Passing-Products-Detection-\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-6f8ba8e6-c701-4264-aa7f-d8e7d0a8bb01').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
